 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "He poured forty gallons of bright white paint onto his roof...",
   "words": [
    0,
    10
   ],
   "subject": "hero"
  },
  {
   "text": "while every single neighbor in the valley coated theirs in thick black tar.",
   "words": [
    11,
    23
   ],
   "subject": "town"
  },
  {
   "text": "Down here, summers hit a hundred and fifteen degrees,",
   "words": [
    24,
    32
   ],
   "subject": "sign"
  },
  {
   "text": "and everyone swears dark tar is the only thing that seals out cracks.",
   "words": [
    33,
    45
   ],
   "subject": "nb"
  },
  {
   "text": "His next-door neighbor yells up,",
   "words": [
    46,
    50
   ],
   "subject": "nb"
  },
  {
   "text": "You're blinding the whole street\u2014and that chalk will wash off by July!",
   "words": [
    51,
    62
   ],
   "subject": "nb"
  },
  {
   "text": "Then August arrives,",
   "words": [
    63,
    65
   ],
   "subject": "town"
  },
  {
   "text": "and the hottest heatwave in fifty years parks right over the town.",
   "words": [
    66,
    77
   ],
   "subject": "town"
  },
  {
   "text": "Inside the black-tar houses, the roofs act like giant frying pans\u2014",
   "words": [
    78,
    88
   ],
   "subject": "roof"
  },
  {
   "text": "soaking up the sun and baking the rooms underneath even at midnight.",
   "words": [
    89,
    100
   ],
   "subject": "nb"
  },
  {
   "text": "Meanwhile, his white roof acts like a mirror,",
   "words": [
    101,
    108
   ],
   "subject": "town"
  },
  {
